\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Three equilibria between two folds}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In the SNLC column of
\citet{Table 3.1, p. 51}{ermentrout2010mathematical}, the rows
that differ from the Hopf column of \ref{fnip-0005} are
#{\phi=0.067}, #{g_{\mathrm{Ca}}=4}, #{V_{3}=12}, and
#{V_{4}=17.4}.
\citet{p. 59}{ermentrout2010mathematical} says that an applied
current between about #{-15} and #{40} gives three equilibria, and
that only the lower one is stable. As that current increases, the
stable [node](fnip-0035) and the [saddle](fnip-0035) meet. Figure
3.6a on p. 60 draws the equilibrium voltage against the current
and labels the two folds.
\citet{§6.1.1, p. 162}{izhikevich2007dynamical} reads the same
meeting off a local maximum or a local minimum of the steady
current.}
